      <h2>Who I am as an engineer</h2>
      <p>
        I’m Andrew Estrada, a mechanical engineer who learned early that drawings only matter if the part can be made, assembled, and proven. That preference for end-to-end ownership shaped my work founding NAU’s Formula SAE program, supporting manufacturing teams in industry, and contributing to high-power rocketry.
      </p>
      <p>
        Across those settings I have owned geometry development, structural analysis, CNC machining, fixture design, quality checks, and test support. Recruiters reviewing this site should expect evidence of CAD proficiency — and also evidence of shop-floor judgment.
      </p>
      <h2>What I’m looking for</h2>
      <p>
        Roles where mechanical design, manufacturing engineering, tooling, test, or product development require someone who can move between the model and the machine. Automotive, aerospace, and adjacent hardware industries are a natural fit.
      </p>
